{"subject":"Microbiology","sourceTitle":"All In One Online","title":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","deckName":"created by tele @Neet_pg_bot::cereb::subject_tests::cereb sub test Microbiology::006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","questions":[{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203932","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":1,"stem":"Virulence of gonococci is due to?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pili"},{"label":"B","text":"Endotoxin"},{"label":"C","text":"Exotoxin"},{"label":"D","text":"None"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Pili","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. A. Pili </span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203934","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":2,"stem":"Transport medium for gonococcus:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pike’s medium"},{"label":"B","text":"Stuart medium"},{"label":"C","text":"VR medium"},{"label":"D","text":"Thayer Martin medium"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Stuart medium","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. B. Stuart medium</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203936","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":3,"stemHtml":"A 25-year-old man presents with urethral discharge for the last three days. A Gram stained smear of the discharge is show in the figure. All of the following are true about the likely etiology except:<br/><img src=\"images/img_5ddc27bc9a534318865ca9d65e591b10.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Virulence factor Pili"},{"label":"B","text":"Intracellular"},{"label":"C","text":"Both catalase and oxidase positive"},{"label":"D","text":"Show tumbling motility"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Show tumbling motility","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. D. Show Tumbling motility</strong></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\">The Gram stain of urethral discharge showing Gram-negative diplococci inside neutrophils is classic for Neisseria gonorrhoeae.</span><br/> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\">N. gonorrhoeae uses type IV pili, which can extend and retract, pulling the bacterium along a surface in a jerky manner  termed as twitching motility</span><br/><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\">It's not flagella-mediated motility rather pili mediated extension and retraction looking like motility</span><br/> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Other options: </strong></span><br/> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Option A. Virulence factor Pili</strong>: True. Pili are critical for attachment to mucosal surfaces and antigenic variation, helping in immune evasion.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Option B. Intracellular</strong>: True. Neisseria gonorrhoeae is often seen intracellularly within neutrophils on Gram stain of urethral or cervical discharge.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Option C. Both catalase and oxidase positive</strong>: True. Neisseria gonorrhoeae is oxidase positive and catalase positive.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Educational Objective: </strong></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\">Neisseria gonorrhoeae (gram-negative intracellular diplococci causing urethral discharge) exhibits twitching motility via type IV pili, NOT tumbling motility which is characteristic of flagellated bacteria like Listeria and E. coli. Remember: \"Gonococcus Twitches with pili, Listeria Tumbles with flagella\" - both oxidase and catalase positive.</span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203938","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":4,"stemHtml":"Mechanism of action of toxin produced by the bacterium shown in the figure:<br/><img src=\"images/img_4a6996c0395543a2b8c8cbddc850ff58.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Increase in cAMP"},{"label":"B","text":"Increase in cGMP"},{"label":"C","text":"ADP-ribosylation of Elongation factor"},{"label":"D","text":"ADP-ribosylation of Gs protein"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"ADP-ribosylation of Elongation factor","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. C. ADP-ribosylation of Elongation factor</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203940","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":5,"stem":"Meningococci differ from gonococci in that they:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Are intracellular"},{"label":"B","text":"Possess a capsule"},{"label":"C","text":"Cause fermentation of glucose"},{"label":"D","text":"Are oxidase positive"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Possess a capsule","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. B. Possess a capsule</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203942","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":6,"stem":"Most common genetic play in Neisseria infection is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Male gender"},{"label":"B","text":"HLA B27"},{"label":"C","text":"Complement deficiency"},{"label":"D","text":"IgA deficiency"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Complement deficiency","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. C. Complement deficiency</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203944","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":7,"stem":"A young lady complains of sore throat for 3 days along with fever and headache. On examination, she was severely dehydrated, her BP was found to be 90/50mm Hg and on the distal aspect of the cuff, small red spots were noted. What could be the most probable etiological agent responsible for causing these symptoms?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Brucella abortus"},{"label":"B","text":"Brucella suis"},{"label":"C","text":"Neisseria meningitidis"},{"label":"D","text":"Staphylococcus aureus"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Neisseria meningitidis","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. C. Neisseria meningitidis</strong></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\">This clinical scenario is highly suggestive of meningococcemia, caused by Neisseria meningitidis. Sore throat, fever, and headache may indicate be early signs of meningococcal infection and Severe dehydration and hypotension indicates septic shock</span></p><p><br/><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\">Small red spots on the distal cuff → Petechial rash, classic for meningococcemia which is due to DIC and capillary hemorrhages</span><br/> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Other options:</strong></span><br/> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Option A &amp; Option B: Brucella abortus / suis</strong> – Cause brucellosis, which presents with undulant fever, malaise, arthralgia – not associated with petechial rash or hypotension.</span><br/> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Option D: Staphylococcus aureus</strong> – Can cause sepsis and toxic shock syndrome, but petechial rash is not a hallmark, and sore throat is not a typical feature.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\"><strong>Educational Objective: </strong></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\">Young patient with sore throat, fever, hypotension, and petechial rash (small red spots) is classic for meningococcemia caused by Neisseria meningitidis, presenting with septic shock and DIC-related hemorrhages. Remember: \"Meningococcus = Medical emergency with petechiae\" - requires immediate antibiotics (ceftriaxone) and supportive care.</span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203946","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":8,"stem":"Capsular polysaccharide derived vaccine is available for all meningococci except?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Group A"},{"label":"B","text":"Group B"},{"label":"C","text":"Group C"},{"label":"D","text":"Group Y"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Group B","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. B. Group B</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203948","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":9,"stem":"Differentiating feature of Neisseria gonococcus from Neisseria meningitidis is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lactose fermentation"},{"label":"B","text":"Maltose fermentation"},{"label":"C","text":"Mannitol fermentation"},{"label":"D","text":"Sucrose fermentation"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Maltose fermentation","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. B. Maltose fermentation</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203950","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":10,"stem":"Where does gonococci initially infect?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vagina"},{"label":"B","text":"Cervix"},{"label":"C","text":"Uterus"},{"label":"D","text":"Fallopian tubes"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Cervix","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. B. Cervix</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203952","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":11,"stem":"Waterhouse-Friderichsen syndrome is seen in:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pneumococci"},{"label":"B","text":"N.meningitidis"},{"label":"C","text":"Pseudomonas"},{"label":"D","text":"Yersinia"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"N.meningitidis","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. B. N.meningitidis</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203954","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":12,"stemHtml":"A child presents to the hospital with fever, sore throat, malaise, and cervical lymphadenopathy. On clinical examination, grey to white exudates is seen in the pharynx. A stain was used and following organism seen. The dye used for staining contains:<br/><img src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/images/2023/07/12/untitled-1001.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Carbolfuschin, acetone, methylene blue"},{"label":"B","text":"Carbolfuschin, acetone, iodine"},{"label":"C","text":"Malachite green, toluidine blue, Iodine"},{"label":"D","text":"Iodine, Brilliant green, acetone"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Malachite green, toluidine blue, Iodine","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. C. Malachite green, toluidine blue, Iodine</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203956","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":13,"stem":"Toxin production by Corynebacterium diphtheriae is due to?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chromosomal mutation"},{"label":"B","text":"Presence of plasmid"},{"label":"C","text":"Lysogenic transversion"},{"label":"D","text":"Transformation"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Lysogenic transversion","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. C. Lysogenic transversion</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203958","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":14,"stem":"True about Corynebacterium diphtheriae:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"All types produce toxin"},{"label":"B","text":"Toxin production is dependent upon critical concentration of iron"},{"label":"C","text":"Coded by plasmid"},{"label":"D","text":"Inhibit Camp"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Toxin production is dependent upon critical concentration of iron","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. B. Toxin production is dependent upon critical concentration of iron </span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203960","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":15,"stem":"A 12-year-old child presents with fever and cervical lymphadenopathy. Oral examination shows a grey membrane on the right tonsil extending to the anterior pillar. Which of the following medium will be ideal for the culture of the throat swab for a rapid identification of the pathogen?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nutrient agar"},{"label":"B","text":"Blood agar"},{"label":"C","text":"Loffler’s serum slope"},{"label":"D","text":"Lowenstein-Jensen medium"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Loffler’s serum slope","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. C. Loffler’s serum slope</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203962","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":16,"stem":"Poached egg colony on tellurite blood agar is produced by which strain of corneybacterium diphtheriae?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gravis"},{"label":"B","text":"Mitis"},{"label":"C","text":"Intermedius"},{"label":"D","text":"Minimus"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Mitis","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. B. Mitis</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203964","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":17,"stem":"Elek’s gel precipitation test used for diagnosing:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Corynebacterium jakeium"},{"label":"B","text":"Corynebacterium diphtheriae"},{"label":"C","text":"Clostridium tetani"},{"label":"D","text":"Clostridium perfringens"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Corynebacterium diphtheriae","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. B. Corynebacterium diphtheriae</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203966","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":18,"stem":"Most common complication of diphtheria is?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Myocarditis"},{"label":"B","text":"Pneumonia"},{"label":"C","text":"Meningitis"},{"label":"D","text":"Endocarditis"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Myocarditis","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. A. Myocarditis </span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203968","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":19,"stem":"Most important element in treatment of diphtheria?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Antitoxin"},{"label":"B","text":"Tetracycline"},{"label":"C","text":"Erythromycin"},{"label":"D","text":"Penicillin"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Antitoxin","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. A. Antitoxin </span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436203970","topic":"Cerebellum · 006-T-20 Microbiology Test-4 - 12-07-2023 - 2023-07-12","number":20,"stem":"Schick test is for?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Susceptibility to diphtheria"},{"label":"B","text":"Susceptibility to tetanus"},{"label":"C","text":"Susceptibility to scarlet fever"},{"label":"D","text":"Susceptibility to RF"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Susceptibility to diphtheria","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Ans. A. Susceptibility to diphtheria</span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""}]}